  info: 'Diptera is an order of insects known as "true flies." Diptera contains over
    150,000 species with some of the more known being house flies, horse flies, mosquitos,
    and gnats. Flies have large, compound eyes and advanced mechanosensory organs
    that allow for quick reflexes and the ability to manuver with ease.


    Source:
    en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fly '
